    {
      "short": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "body": [
        "<ul class=\"takeaways\">\n          <li>Put servers and keys on a <b>hash ring</b>; a key belongs to the <b>next server clockwise</b>.</li>\n          <li>Adding or removing a server moves only <b>one arc</b> — about 1/N of keys.</li>\n          <li><b>Virtual nodes</b> even out shares and spread the load when servers leave.</li>\n          <li>Store each key on the <b>next N servers</b> clockwise for redundancy.</li>\n        </ul>"
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "next",
        "text": "Next up: <b>Unique IDs at Scale</b> — giving every row a name once there is no single database to count for you."
